      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I\u0027ll add that.  Thanks.\n\nBy the way, as you probably noticed, this code is a bit over-simplistic in that it just undoes the patch on every 4 bytes in the .text section, instead of using the .eh_frame section to ignore parts of .text that shouldn\u0027t be patched, as the kernel does (https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android14-6.1/arch/arm64/kernel/patch-scs.c).  This was enough to get the integrity check passing.  Let me know if you think the .eh_frame parsing should be implemented now anyway.  I think it\u0027s complex enough that we should leave it out until it\u0027s shown to be needed in some case.",
